# Copy this file to .env (same directory) and fill in the real flag
# before running `docker compose up --build`.
#
# .env itself is listed in .gitignore and must never be committed —
# this .env.example file (placeholder only) is the only version that
# belongs in git. See docs/operations.mdx's "Image-layer handling of
# the flag" section for why the flag still ends up baked into the built
# image's layers regardless of how it reaches the build arg, and why
# that is an accepted trade-off only because the built image itself is
# never distributed or pushed anywhere.

FLAG=duck{replace_with_the_real_flag_before_building}
